{"agent_id":"pp3g-qN6T-write-the-consolidated-workflow-topology-design-0521","agent_seq":5,"timestamp":"2026-08-08T00:44:37.326047639Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"1e9ad7ce-cdec-41f3-9487-f292dc8f789a","comment_uuid":"d9ff85ef-4cfe-4fe5-84e5-d10d6a2fa041","author":"pp3g-qN6T-write-the-consolidated-workflow-topology-design-0521","content":"## RESULT: Consolidated WORKFLOW-TOPOLOGY design + reasoning record (gh#254)\n\nCommitted 40f7d21. Document: **docs/research/Workflow Topology Design and Reasoning Record.md** (795 lines, EDASES frontmatter: program=EDASES, layer=Research, document_type=Synthesis, status=Active, authority=Experimental).\n\n### What the doc captures\n\n1. **Two principles** — (a) reasoning certainty (WHY/WHAT/HOW-CERTAIN/WHAT-NOT-TESTED) with the carrier gap (hy3 F2/C6); (b) cheapest-test-first with the falsifying-vs-discriminating source-fidelity finding (hy3 F1, HIGH) and the operator resolution; trilemma/regress handling (GLM C1/C2).\n2. **Topology finding** — information-asymmetry boundary as dominant unguarded failure point, grounded in the #154/#232 binary-vs-source misattribution (E3 parity test); honest scope limits (hy3 F3: no-claim/brief-borne/multi-hop blind spots; GLM F7/C6 inversions); role-justification criterion (distinct capability/authority + distinct failure class).\n3. **Finalized workflow design** — position-emitting agents + durable store + task-adaptive cadence; cheap staleness trigger (logical trigger set enumerated); AUDITOR as ONE-role/TWO-PHASE in-flight divergence verifier (in-flight monitor vs post-hoc audit, model variation across phases, no duplicate Verifier per operator decision); orchestrator as single integration point (operator supervises orchestrator); reviewer = pre-consumption readiness audit; full first-wave condition→resolution mapping table (GLM F1-F7+C1-C6, luna F1-F6, hy3 C1-C8).\n4. **Model-agreement collection** — finding-level agreement (load-bearing, #154 R1 B2), external correctness anchor (F11), non-delivery as first-class outcome (F12), granular back-fill confidence, honest zero-cost framing (F10/GLM F5).\n5. **Reasoning trail** — 5 discussion arcs with question/evidence/argument/decision structure: auditor underuse & re-positioning, no-new-role decision (kimi #252 resolution), operator-thinness invariant, agreement-as-byproduct, 504 long-verdict finding.\n\nPlus: review wave record (first wave #242-245 verdict matrix; delta wave #250-252 incl. kimi DISAGREE and its operator resolution), 10 explicitly-open items, and full evidence base.\n\n### Notes\n- Model-agreement schema/backfill (#241, commit 5c92e9d) are DRAFT on an unmerged sibling branch — referenced with that status; this doc links them as dependencies without treating them as canonical.\n- Authority=Experimental: the design is operator-finalized; canonicalization into ASES methodology docs is a downstream step (role-doc updates per the kimi 'redefine, do not imply' rule are listed as open item #10).","created_at":"2026-08-08T00:44:37.320348745Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:bDT3e8E2LRwXyS5XCZidO5GA+3Jl8p2WCbXM2UhrClc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgUoLNCr1YgQdmbC6vGROcgLtB02E22Dsb2Vxrd09eI3cAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAPBVwiXuI0jsx8IglnCV6A3aENVZEUFt9vl27n31MBtbrUNOopAmXH27132KTWo21eNN//cU4ceA6ljQCuACxCQ=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:bDT3e8E2LRwXyS5XCZidO5GA+3Jl8p2WCbXM2UhrClc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgUoLNCr1YgQdmbC6vGROcgLtB02E22Dsb2Vxrd09eI3cAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQKC4VJ0q0MC1zByoqM624bFs+IXRoCAicL3+v1JwmDsnAdhIj0AJxKM86KHvR5IbKPvixsu+1nqhBvvoK2P8YQk="}
